# Product: YouTube Video Creation & Upload Tool

Professional desktop application (Tauri + Vue 3) for creating YouTube-ready videos from audio files and images, with integrated upload management, audio processing, and Discogs metadata integration.

## Core Features

### 🎬 Video Creation
- **Bulk video creation** — Pair multiple audio tracks with images; batch-create 1920×1080 MP4s in parallel
- **Flexible image sources** — Local files, folder images, image URLs, or Discogs release artwork
- **Multiple image styles**:
  - Automatic (centered crop with blurred background)
  - Fit 16:9 (contain or cover modes)
  - Custom background (main image + custom background)
  - Background-only (no main image, just background)
- **Predefined backgrounds** — Library of built-in background templates with favorites
- **Smart image assignment** — Per-track assignment, "use previous track's image", or apply same image to all tracks
- **Real-time preview** — Preview processed images before video creation
- **Audio metadata extraction** — Automatically extracts artist, title, album, and album art from audio files
- **Auto-assign album art** — Uses embedded album art when available
- **Progress tracking** — Real-time progress per video with detailed status (image processing, encoding, completion)
- **Parallel rendering** — Multiple videos created simultaneously (up to 4 concurrent)

### 📤 YouTube Upload
- **Bulk upload** — Upload multiple videos simultaneously with individual progress tracking
- **Rich metadata** — Titles, descriptions, tags, categories, privacy settings, made-for-kids flag
- **Privacy options** — Public, unlisted, private, or save as draft
- **Scheduling** — Schedule private videos to go public at a specific date/time
- **Playlist assignment** — Automatically add videos to YouTube playlists
- **Video thumbnails** — Automatic thumbnail generation from video files
- **OAuth authentication** — Secure YouTube API authentication with token management
- **Resumable uploads** — Large file uploads with progress tracking and resumption
- **Upload history** — Track all uploads with search, filtering, and pagination
- **Processing status** — Check YouTube video processing status (uploaded, processing, processed, failed)
- **Video links** — Direct links to uploaded videos and their processing status

### 🎵 Audio Normalization
- **Standalone normalization** — Normalize audio files independently of video creation
- **During video creation** — Optional normalization step before video encoding
- **EBU R128 loudnorm** — Professional loudness normalization (-16 LUFS integrated loudness)
- **Peak adjustment** — True peak (-0.5 dBTP) and final peak (-0.1 dB) adjustment
- **High-pass filtering** — Optional 30Hz high-pass filter to remove low-frequency noise
- **Parallel processing** — Process multiple files simultaneously using all CPU cores
- **USB-compatible output** — Optimized for USB playback (WAV 44.1kHz/16-bit stereo)
- **Output options** — Overwrite originals or add suffix to filenames

### 🎨 Discogs Integration
- **OAuth authentication** — Secure Discogs API authentication
- **Release search** — Search Discogs releases with autocomplete (debounced)
- **Release linking** — Link releases to videos for metadata auto-fill
- **Bulk linking** — Link one release to multiple videos at once
- **Metadata auto-fill** — Auto-populate title, description, and tags from Discogs releases
- **Description templates** — Customizable description template builder with Discogs tags (artist, release, year, label, catalog number, genres, styles, URL)
- **Image selection** — Use Discogs release artwork as video images during creation
- **Release information** — Display full release details (artists, labels, year, genres, styles, tracklist)

### ⚙️ Settings & Preferences
- **Default image style** — Set default image processing style for new tracks
- **Default fit mode** — Set default fit mode (contain/cover) for fit-16x9 style
- **Default background** — Set favorite predefined background
- **Default privacy** — Set default YouTube privacy status (public/private/unlisted/draft)
- **Default category** — Set default YouTube category
- **Default playlist** — Set default YouTube playlist for uploads
- **Default normalization** — Enable normalization by default during video creation
- **Default high-pass** — Enable high-pass filter by default when normalizing
- **Output paths** — Remember last used output folders and set preferred output path
- **Description templates** — Build reusable description templates with tags and custom text
- **Notifications** — Desktop notifications on upload completion (with permission management)
- **Account management** — Connect/disconnect YouTube and Discogs accounts
- **Data management** — Clear all app data (preferences, history, tokens)

### 📊 Upload History
- **Complete tracking** — All uploads saved with metadata (title, YouTube URL, Discogs link)
- **Search & filter** — Search by title or Discogs release title
- **Pagination** — Browse large upload histories efficiently
- **Processing status** — Real-time status checking (uploaded, processing, processed, failed, deleted)
- **Status sync** — Manual and automatic status refresh
- **Direct links** — Open YouTube videos and Discogs releases directly

## Stack

- **Frontend**: Vue 3 (Composition API), ShadCn-style UI components, Tailwind CSS
- **Backend**: Rust with clean architecture (domain/use-cases/infrastructure pattern)
- **Video/Audio Processing**: FFmpeg (command-line, bundled or system)
- **Image Processing**: Rust `image` crate (centered crop, blur, brightness/contrast adjustments)
- **Platform**: Tauri (cross-platform desktop: macOS, Linux, Windows)
- **Storage**: Tauri Store plugin for persistent preferences and upload history
- **OAuth**: Local callback server for YouTube and Discogs authentication

## User Flow

### Video Creation Flow
1. **Source selection** — Pick audio files (individual files or folder) with automatic metadata extraction
2. **Image assignment** — For each track, assign image (file/folder/URL/Discogs) and choose style
3. **Preview** — See real-time preview of processed images
4. **Audio options** — Enable normalization and high-pass filter if needed
5. **Output** — Choose output folder (remembers last used)
6. **Create** — Batch create videos with parallel processing and per-video progress

### YouTube Upload Flow
1. **Authentication** — Connect YouTube account (OAuth flow)
2. **Source selection** — Pick video files (individual files or folder)
3. **Metadata editing** — Set title, description, tags, category, privacy for each video
4. **Discogs linking** (optional) — Search and link Discogs releases for auto-fill
5. **Template application** — Apply description templates with Discogs data
6. **Upload** — Bulk upload with progress tracking and automatic history saving

### Audio Normalization Flow
1. **Source selection** — Pick audio files (individual files or folder)
2. **Output selection** — Choose output folder
3. **Options** — Enable high-pass filter, choose overwrite or suffix
4. **Normalize** — Process files in parallel with progress tracking
